    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville-Victoria/Casual-Academics---Melbourne-Dental-School_JR-017697-1": {
      "title": "Casual Academics - Melbourne Dental School",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nVariable time\n\nRole type:   Casual; Sessional academic   Faculty:   Faculty of Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences   Department / School:   Melbourne Dental School   Salary:   Casual   sessional   academic rates as per University of Melbourne Enterprise Agreement, plus   1 2 % super     Shape the next generation of   oral health practitioners by   teaching    in   the   D octor of Dental Surgery (D DS ) ,   Bachelor of Oral Health ( BOH ) , and Doctor of Clinical Dentistry (DCD)   program s   at   Melbourne Dental   School   / Enjoy flexible, sessional academic work. Apply now to grow your clinical teaching   expertise   while guiding safe, evidence-based dental care for diverse patients       The University of Melbourne     We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to   benefit   society through the transformative impact of education and research.   Discover more via our website.   Your next career opportunity     You will play a key role in developing   dental and oral health therapy   students’ clinical competence and professional judgement.   You will supervise preclinical and clinical activities at   the   Melbourne Dental School , guiding safe, high-quality care for diverse patients.   You will also build your own teaching skills within a collaborative,   values -driven dental school community.     What you will deliver:     Prepare for preclinical and clinical teaching sessions, reviewing materials, patient   records   and   logistics   to support   evidence based   learning.   Supervise,   guide   and educate   students during preclinical and clinical sessions, focusing on skills acquisition and knowledge application.   Review and approve patient dental records and   clinic    documentation , ensuring   accurate , compliant clinical records for every session.   Facilitate student feedback discussions and complete required assessment, marking,   questionnaires   and sessional administrative documentation.   Participate in meetings,   training   and compliance activities to   maintain   credentialing, child   safety   and high-quality teaching standards.     You may be a great fit   if   you :     Hold a primary dental qualification, eligible for registration with the Dental Board of Australia.   Bring at least   two   years’ clinical experience   (varies between programs) , with strong, contemporary evidence-based dental practice skills.   Maintain current   Ahpra   registration with no conditions, and   clinic   credentialing   appropriate to   clinical teaching   on the MDS teaching clinics. Demonstrate strong motivation to develop excellence in dental education,   assessment   and student feedback.   Work effectively both independently and collaboratively, contributing positively to diverse students,   patients   and academic colleagues.   Exhibit well-developed communication and interpersonal skills, supporting students’ learning in complex preclinical and clinical environments.   For further   information   please refer to the attached   job duties   description .       Your new team –   Melbourne Dental School   At the Melbourne Dental School, you will join a values-driven community within the Faculty of Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences. The   School   partners closely with the Royal Dental Hospital of Melbourne   (RDHM) , delivering high-impact clinical education and patient care. You will collaborate with skilled clinicians and educators who champion evidence-based practice,   innovation   and student success, while enjoying   strong support   for your professional development and wellbeing.     Be   y ourself     The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe   organisation . The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences.   Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb.   We're   committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities.   Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process .   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander   a pplicants     We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians.   Visit   our   Indigenous staff page   to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.           Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at   korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au .     Application essentials:   Visit   \"apply with us\"   to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.   You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.   A Working with Children Check is   required   for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.    Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process.  Want to know more?   For queries related to this specific position, contact   mds-operations@unimelb.edu.au     For questions related to our recruitment process email   hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at   hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').     Apply   today, and   join a community   that’s   shaping the future.   Job Duties Description – Doctor of Dental Surgery (DDS).pdf Job   Duties   Description – Bachelor of Oral Health   (BOH)   ( Coming   Soon)   Job   Duties   Description – Doctor of   Clinical   Dentistry   (DCD)   ( Coming   soon )"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville/Expressions-of-Interest--Indigenous-Employment-Opportunities-at-the-University-of-Melbourne_JR-006839": {
      "title": "Expressions of Interest: Indigenous Employment Opportunities at the University of Melbourne",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe University of Melbourne is inviting Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander candidates to submit an Expression of Interest (EOI) for current and future opportunities across both professional and academic positions. Whether you are just starting your career or seeking the next step in your professional or academic journey, we encourage you to express your interest in joining our vibrant and diverse community. You may express interest in the following professional areas: Finance | Call Centre & Customer Service | Student Support Services | HR, Recruitment & Culture | Legal | Fundraising | Administration & Office Support | Management Roles | Strategy, Culture & Analytics | Information & Communications Technology | Marketing & Communications You may express interest in the following academic roles across all faculties: Tutor | Research Assistant | Research Fellow | Lecturer | Associate Professor Only Indigenous Australians are eligible to apply as these positions are exempt under the Special Measure Provision, Section 12 (1) of the Equal Opportunity Act 2011 (Vic).  The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfillment, including:  Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being  Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance, including Cultural Leave  Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance  Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program with access to Indigenous counsellors for Indigenous staff Dedicated and ongoing support from Korin Korin, our Indigenous Employment and Development team A vibrant and active Indigenous Staff Network, providing opportunities for connection and professional development For more information check out our benefits page!  Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. We believe the diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing reasonable adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. For assistance, please contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments'). Contact details for other enquiries are located at the bottom of this page. Find more information for applicants requiring reasonable adjustments. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. outlines our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff and students.    Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with Korin Korin, at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au for further information and support.  Our Indigenous strategy, Murmuk Djerring outlines our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff and students.   Please note : This role requires current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available.   A Working with Children Check (WWCC) is required for all positions. If successful, we'll guide you through the WWCC application process during onboarding and reimburse the cost. Join Us and unlock your career potential!   If this role is right for you, please apply with the following documents:  Resume   Cover Letter outlining your interest and experience Proof of Aboriginality Please note: As part of the application, you’ll be asked to share your preferences for the types of roles and levels of experience that best match your background. For recruitment queries, email Olivia korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au . Include the Position Number and Job Title in the subject line. Please do not send applications to this email address."
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Early-Childhood-Educator-s---Teacher-s--Casual-Positions_JR-016427": {
      "title": "Early Childhood Educators & Teachers, Casual Positions",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-07\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\n\nPlease apply via this link: https://careers.giighire.com/universityofmelbourne/29027?source=link DO NOT APPLY VIA THE UOM CAREERS PAGE Role type: Casual positions Department : Student and Scholarly services Support high-quality early learning / collaborate in inclusive, research-informed practice / join a respected University childcare service Apply now to contribute your expertise in early childhood education across our vibrant University children’s centres. Investing in you – health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities. The University of Melbourne We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website.   Your next career opportunity You will support high-quality early childhood programs across our University centres, grounded in evidence-based pedagogy. You will collaborate with experienced colleagues to create inclusive, play-based learning that strengthens every child’s wellbeing. You will gain varied experience supporting different age groups, rooms, and services within a child-safe organisation.   What you will deliver: Plan, implement, and evaluate play-based learning programs aligned with EYLF, VEYLDF, and service philosophies. Document children’s learning, development, and wellbeing to inform individual planning and continuous programme improvement. Maintain safe, inclusive environments through active supervision, risk management, and adherence to all regulatory requirements. Build strong, respectful relationships with children, families, and colleagues to support belonging and collaborative practice. Collaborate with room leaders and teams to reflect on practice and support service quality improvement.   You may be a great fit if you: Hold an approved Early Childhood degree and current WWCC or VIT registration. Demonstrate sound knowledge of NQF, National Law and Regulations, and Victorian Child Safe Standards. Bring proven experience delivering high-quality education and care using EYLF, VEYLDF, and evidence-based pedagogies. Create inclusive, stimulating environments that promote children’s agency, participation, and strong sense of belonging. Apply diligent risk management, active supervision, and child-safe practices in dynamic early childhood settings. Adapt flexibly across rooms, age groups, and teams while maintaining professional, collaborative conduct.   For further information please refer to the attached PD.   What we offer you! We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including: Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program   For more information check out our benefits page!   Your new team – Student and Scholarly Services Student and Scholarly Services supports students and staff from first enquiry through to graduation and beyond. Early Childhood Education Services operates three high-quality University children’s centres, delivering evidence-based programmes for infants to preschoolers. You will join a collaborative, research-informed team committed to child safety, inclusion, and continuous quality improvement.   Be Yourself The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb.   We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process.   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants  We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.    Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au .   Application essentials: Please ensure to apply through this link We will NOT be accepting applications through the UOM Careers Page You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience to the link provided as part of the application process. Please apply via this link: https://careers.giighire.com/universityofmelbourne/29027?source=link DO NOT APPLY VIA THE UOM CAREERS PAGE   Position Description: Early Childhood Educator’s & Teacher’s - Casual Positions.docx Early Childhood Educator’s & Teacher’s - Casual Positions.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Lecturer--Indigenous-Social-Equity-and-Leadership---Expression-of-Interest_JR-014395": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Indigenous Social Equity and Leadership - Expression of Interest",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe University of Melbourne is inviting Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander candidates to submit an Expression of Interest (EOI) for a lecturer, Indigenous Social Equity and Leadership position on a full-time continuing basis. This opportunity is offered at Academic Level B, with a salary range of $124,656–$148,023 per annum, plus 17% superannuation. Only Indigenous Australians are eligible to apply as this position is exempt under the Special Measure Provision, Section 12 (1) of the Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic).   Your next career opportunity:   You will design, teach and assess postgraduate subjects in Social Change Leadership for diverse experienced Fellows. You will advance research on Indigenous social change while supporting Fellows’ community-led projects and long-term leadership journeys. You will collaborate across the University and global Atlantic Fellows network to grow your academic and impact profile.  What you will deliver:   Design, deliver and coordinate engaging postgraduate subjects, using culturally grounded, flexible teaching approaches for adult learners.  Supervise and support Fellows to develop rigorous social change project proposals with strong community partnerships and ethical foundations.  Conduct and publish high-quality research on Indigenous social change and leadership, securing external funding where appropriate.  Contribute to AFSE’s research, seminars and public engagement, representing AFSE locally, nationally and internationally.  Build and sustain collaborations with Indigenous communities, partners and University colleagues to strengthen AFSE’s teaching and impact.    You may be a great fit if you:   Hold a doctoral qualification, or be near completion, in a field related to Indigenous social change.  Demonstrate experience co-designing curriculum that embeds Indigenous knowledges, cultural safety principles and decolonial teaching practices.  Show a strong record, or clear potential, in research, publication and collaborative project development.  Exhibit excellence in teaching adult learners, including experienced leaders, using inclusive and reflexive pedagogical approaches.  Work effectively within small, interdisciplinary teams, contributing constructively to programme development and shared strategic priorities.  Engage confidently with Indigenous communities and partners, nurturing ethical, long-term relationships that support social change.  Your new team:   Atlantic Fellows for Social Equity You will join the Atlantic Fellows for Social Equity, a collaborative programme advancing Indigenous and Pacific-led social change. AFSE combines a rich Foundation year of fellowship and postgraduate study while nurturing a lifelong community of senior Fellows. The team works closely with communities, partners and a global Atlantic Fellows network to amplify impact. You will collaborate with committed colleagues across the University, including the Faculty of Education, benefiting from strong mentoring and development opportunities.  Be Yourself    The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences.  Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb.   We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities.  Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process.   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants    We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our  Indigenous staff page  to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.        Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at  oied-hr@unimelb.edu.au .   Application essentials:   Visit  \"apply with us\"  to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.  You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.   A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.   Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application. Want to know more?   For queries related to this expression of interest, please contact Program Director, Dr. Yvonne Ualesi at yvonne.ualesi@unimelb.edu.au      Position Description: PD_JR-014395 EOI Lecturer Indigenous Social Equity and Leadership.docx"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville/Associate-Professor-in-Periodontics_JR-009367-1": {
      "title": "Professor in Periodontics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRole type:  Part-time (0.8 FTE) to Full-time; Continuing Faculty:  Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences School:  Melbourne Dental School Salary: Level D: AUD $183,859 - $202,556 p.a.              Level E: AUD $236,824 p.a.              plus 17% super and clinical loading of AUD $13,494 p.a. International leadership in specialist Periodontics / Shape a nationally benchmarked Doctor of Clinical Dentistry (DCD) Periodontics program / Drive impactful translational research Join us to lead specialist Periodontics education, research and clinical innovation that advances oral health globally. Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.  The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. Your next career opportunity   You will lead the Doctor of Clinical Dentistry (DCD) Periodontics program, integrating specialist clinical training, cutting-edge research and curriculum innovation. You will shape national and international standards in Periodontics while mentoring the next generation of specialist clinicians. What you will deliver:   Lead the design, delivery and evaluation of the DCD Periodontics curriculum and assessment across clinical and academic components. Provide high-quality clinical supervision and safe patient care at RDHM, modelling evidence-based, multidisciplinary specialist Periodontics practice. Establish and lead an internationally recognised research program in Periodontics, securing competitive funding and collaborative partnerships. Supervise and mentor higher degree and postgraduate research students, building research capacity across the discipline and School. Provide strategic leadership in national curriculum frameworks, accreditation standards and professional guidelines for specialist Periodontics. You may be a great fit if you:   Hold and maintain current or clearly eligible specialist AHPRA registration in Periodontics, without limiting conditions or restrictions. Possess a completed PhD in Periodontics or a closely related field, with strong academic credentials. Demonstrate strategic leadership in specialist clinical teaching, including curriculum design, assessment, benchmarking and educational innovation. Show a sustained record of high-quality research, including competitive grant success and impactful translational outcomes. Bring extensive experience supervising higher degree and postgraduate research students through to successful thesis completion. Engage confidently with national and international professional bodies, accreditation panels and multidisciplinary clinical partners. For further information please refer to the attached Candidate Information Pack .  What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:  Build future financial security with 17% superannuation Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being  Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company  Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program  For more information check out our benefits page!  Your new team – “Melbourne Dental School”   You will join the Melbourne Dental School, a leader in specialist dental education and translational research. Working closely with the Royal Dental Hospital of Melbourne, you will help deliver world-class patient-centred clinical training. You will collaborate in a values-driven Faculty of Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences, committed to Advancing Health 2030. Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.    Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au   Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description. Want to know more? For queries related to this specific position, contact Professor Petros Papagerakis or Professor Ivan Darby at the details listed in the position description. For questions related to our recruitment process email Shabon Nawabi at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments'). Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future. Applications close: Friday 9th October 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.  Position Description:   Candidate Information Pack - Professor in Periodontics.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville-Victoria/Senior-Partnership-and-Engagement-Manager--MEC_JR-018267": {
      "title": "Senior Partnership and Engagement Manager, MEC",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-18\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRole type: Full-time; Fixed-term (2 years)   Department: Melbourne Entrepreneurial Centre, Melbourne Enterprise   Salary: UOM 9 - $146,049 - $151,951 p.a. plus 17% super   Senior leadership role in a growing entrepreneurial centre / build strategic corporate and philanthropic partnerships / shape MEC 2030 impact   Join MEC to lead partnerships, community engagement and events that fuel Melbourne’s entrepreneurial ecosystem and venture success.   Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.       The University of Melbourne     We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website.   Your next career opportunity:   In this senior role, you will lead MEC’s partnerships, community and events functions to drive sustainable growth.   You will cultivate corporate and philanthropic partners while energising a vibrant network of students, alumni, mentors and innovators.   What you will deliver:   Lead MEC’s commercial and philanthropic partnerships strategy, pipeline and portfolio to grow revenue and strategic relationships.   Build and activate MEC’s community, alumni and mentor networks to support programs and entrepreneurial engagement.   Oversee a high-quality events program that showcases MEC, strengthens partnerships and deepens community connections.   Provide inclusive leadership, clear direction and coaching to partnerships and engagement staff within a growing team.   Monitor performance, budgets and risk, delivering regular reports on revenue, engagement metrics and partnership impact.     You may be a great fit if you:   Demonstrate a strong record securing corporate and philanthropic partnerships with measurable revenue and relationship outcomes.   Apply commercial acumen to build and manage partnership pipelines, forecasts and stakeholder reporting in complex organisations.   Design and deliver stakeholder, community or alumni engagement programs that deepen long-term participation and advocacy.   Lead and coach professional staff, fostering collaborative, high-performance cultures aligned with shared goals.   Plan and deliver impactful events, from intimate partner engagements to large-scale showcases, with excellent participant experiences.   Engage confidently with entrepreneurship and start-up ecosystems, using data and insights to improve programs and partnerships.     What we offer you!     We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:     Build future financial security with 17% superannuation   Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being     Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning   Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance  and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave   Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company     Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program       For more information check out our benefits page!     Your new team:   Melbourne Entrepreneurial Centre (MEC) is the University’s hub for entrepreneurship, supporting students, researchers and alumni to build ventures.   MEC sits within Melbourne Enterprise and Melbourne Research and Enterprise, connecting deeply with faculties and industry partners.   Based at Melbourne Connect, you will join a collaborative team scaling programs, partnerships, community and impact.   Be Yourself     The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb .   We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process .   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants     We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.        Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au .    Application essentials:   Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.   You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.    A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.    Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process.      Want to know more?   For queries related to this specific position, contact Monica Bulla-Valencia   at monicab@unimelb.edu.au   For questions related to our recruitment process email Alessandro Storani at Alessandro.storani@unimelb.edu.au     For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').      Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future.   Applications close: ​ Sunday 11 October 2026 - 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.    Position Description:     PD_JR-018267 Senior Partnership &amp; Engagement Manager, MEC.pdf PD_JR-018267 Senior Partnership &amp; Engagement Manager, MEC.docx"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville-Victoria/Associate-Director-Graduate-Research_JR-018497": {
      "title": "Associate Director Graduate Research",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nRole type: Full-time; Continuing  Department: Chancellery, Melbourne Research & Enterprise Portfolio  Salary: Senior Manager 1 - an attractive remuneration package p.a. including up to17% super  Influential graduate research leadership role, providing strategic advice on policy, quality and excellence, in collaboration with senior leaders and faculties  Step into a pivotal leadership role and advance graduate research excellence, policy and experience across the University. Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.    The University of Melbourne    We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. Your next career opportunity    In this role, you will play a pivotal role in graduate research strategy, policy and quality assurance across the University. You will advise senior leaders, coordinate institution-wide initiatives and enhance the experience and outcomes of graduate researchers. What you will deliver:   Lead and develop a high-performing professional team, fostering a collaborative, inclusive and service-focused culture. Provide strategic advice on graduate research policy, regulation, quality assurance and sector developments to senior leaders. Design, implement and review graduate research strategies, policies and frameworks that support institutional objectives and compliance. Oversee quality assurance, program evaluation and continuous improvement of research training, supervision and researcher experience. Lead complex, cross-University projects and issues, ensuring effective stakeholder engagement, risk management and timely resolution.   You may be a great fit if you:   Bring deep understanding of contemporary graduate research, supervision practice and higher education sector trends. Apply advanced analytical skills to interpret complex data, identify trends and develop evidence-based recommendations. Possess significant experience managing complex programs or portfolios, including planning, implementation, evaluation and reporting. Provide high-level strategic advice, policy papers and executive briefings for senior governance and leadership audiences. Demonstrate proven success leading and developing professional teams through change, performance management and capability building. Hold a postgraduate qualification in higher education, education, public policy, research management or related discipline. For further information please refer to the attached PD.  What we offer you!    We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:  Build future financial security with 17% superannuation Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being  Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company  Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program  For more information check out our benefits page!  Your new team – “Melbourne Research & Enterprise Portfolio”    You will join Chancellery’s Melbourne Research & Enterprise portfolio, home to the University’s research leadership and support. The Office of the Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Research) partners with faculties and institutes to drive Strategy 2030 and Advancing Research 2030, strengthen research training and enhance impact. You will work closely with the Pro Vice-Chancellor (Graduate Research) and a committed professional team, in a collaborative environment that values evidence-based decision-making, innovation and continuous improvement.    Be Yourself    The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants    We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.        Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au   Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.  Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process.  Want to know more? For queries related to this specific position or our recruitment process, email Ethan Khamly at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').  Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future. Applications close: Tuesday 13th October 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.  Position Description:   JR-018497 Associate Director Graduate Research .docx   JR-018497 Associate Director Graduate Research .pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Werribee/Equine-Veterinary-Nurse_JR-017945-1": {
      "title": "Equine Veterinary Nurse",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nRole type:  Full-time; Continuing Faculty:  Science Department/School:  Melbourne Veterinary School – Werribee Equine Centre Salary:  UoM 4: $80,400 - $85,328 p.a. plus 17% super Renowned equine teaching hospital environment / varied hospital and ambulatory caseload / strong focus on education and growth Step into a leading equine teaching hospital and grow your nursing career supporting complex, meaningful cases. Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.  The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. Your next career opportunity   As an Equine Veterinary Nurse, you will provide high quality care in hospital and ambulatory settings. You will support specialist clinicians, mentor DVM students and contribute to a leading equine teaching hospital. What you will deliver:   Provide high quality equine nursing care, including horse handling, restraint, treatment support and ongoing inpatient husbandry. Assist veterinarians with diagnostics, surgery, anaesthesia, and emergency care, ensuring thorough preparation and post procedure monitoring. Maintain clinical equipment, stocks, and records, upholding rigorous biosecurity, infection control and workplace safety standards. Support delivery of ambulatory services by preparing vehicles, equipment and providing nursing assistance during farm visits. Guide DVM students in practical equine nursing, horse handling and professional behaviour within a supportive teaching environment. You may be a great fit if you:   Hold a Diploma or Certificate IV in Veterinary Nursing, or equivalent experience, ideally with equine focus. Bring proven equine veterinary nursing and horse handling experience within a clinical practice or hospital environment. Demonstrate strong organisational skills, with ability to manage competing priorities and follow detailed clinical protocols. Apply sound knowledge of animal welfare, infection control, biosecurity and safe large animal handling practices. Use veterinary practice software and animal care databases confidently to support accurate records and billing. Value working in a collaborative teaching hospital, supporting veterinarians and mentoring veterinary students. For further information please refer to the attached PD.  What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:  Build future financial security with 17% superannuation Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being  Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company  Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program  For more information check out our benefits page!  Your new team – Melbourne Veterinary School Melbourne Veterinary School, in the Faculty of Science, is a highly ranked leader in veterinary education. The Werribee Equine Centre delivers specialist referral, primary care and ambulatory services as a leading equine teaching hospital. Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.    Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au . Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process. Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description. Learn more about responding to Selection Criteria Want to know more? For queries related to this specific position, contact Carina Wickens (Details in Position Description) For questions related to our recruitment process email Lachlan Bryce at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments'). Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future. Applications close: 19 October 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.  Position Description:   JR-017945 Equine Veterinary Nurse_PD.pdf JR-017945 Equine Veterinary Nurse_PD.docx"
