    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville/Academic-Positions--Level-B--C-or-D--Education---Research-Indigenous-Law-and-Justice-Hub_JR-018041-1": {
      "title": "Academic Positions (Level B, C or D) Education & Research Indigenous Law and Justice Hub",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nRole type:  Full time, Continuing Faculty: Melbourne Law School / Indigenous Law and Justice Hub Salary: UoM B - $124,656 - $148,023 p.a. plus 17% super UoM C - $152,695 - $176,065 p.a. plus 17% super UoM D - $183,859 - $202,556 p.a. plus 17% super  Champion Indigenous legal scholarship and advocacy / shape culturally safe curricula and research partnerships / collaborate with First Nations scholars Apply now to help redefine legal education and research through Indigenous knowledge, leadership and community partnerships. Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.  Only Indigenous Australians are eligible to apply as this position is exempt under the Special Measure Provision, Section 12 (1) of the Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic).     The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. Your next career opportunity   Melbourne Law School invites applications for an academic position within the Indigenous Law and Justice Hub. The level of appointment will be commensurate with the successful applicant’s qualifications, experience and academic profile. The successful applicant will contribute to the School’s teaching, research, engagement, leadership and service, bringing expertise in any area of law relevant to the work of the Indigenous Law and Justice Hub. What you will deliver:   Teaching in the Melbourne Juris Doctor, Melbourne Law Masters and, where appropriate, undergraduate Breadth programs. Contributing to curriculum and subject development, particularly in relation to law and Indigenous peoples. Supervising coursework and/or higher degree research students, as appropriate to level and experience. Undertaking high-quality, nationally and internationally significant legal research and publishing in leading outlets. Contributing to research projects, grant activity and knowledge exchange. Supporting an engaging, inclusive and high-quality student learning experience. Building relationships and partnerships through the Indigenous Law and Justice Hub and contributing to community and professional engagement. Contributing to the collegial life, leadership and service of Melbourne Law School and the University, with more senior appointments expected to make a significant contribution to Indigenous strategy and cultural capability. You may be a great fit if you:   A strong academic background in law and relevant postgraduate qualifications, including a PhD or equivalent (or equivalent professional experience where applicable). A developing, established or internationally recognised record of legal research and publication, commensurate with level. Teaching experience and a commitment to high-quality legal education and student outcomes. The capacity to contribute to research, engagement, leadership and service. A commitment to collegiality, diversity and inclusion, and maintaining a culturally safe workplace. Relevant professional experience, networks and/or expertise in legal education and educational technologies will be highly regarded. Applicants should identify the academic level for which they are applying and demonstrate their suitability against the relevant criteria. For further information please refer to the attached PD.  What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:  Build future financial security with 17% superannuation Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being  Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company  Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program  For more information check out our benefits page!  Your new team – Melbourne Law School The Indigenous Law and Justice Hub brings together Indigenous leaders, legal scholars and communities to advance justice. Based within Melbourne Law School, the Hub embeds Indigenous knowledges across teaching, research, engagement and student support. You will join a values‑driven, empathetic and collaborative team committed to cultural safety and community‑led priorities.  Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff. Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au . Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process. Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description. Want to know more? For queries related to this specific position, contact Nicole Watson at nicole.watson.1@unimelb.edu.au For questions related to our recruitment process email Nick Petersen at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments'). Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future. Applications close: Sunday 18 October 2026 at 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.  Position Description: MLS Academic Recruitment 2026 Indigenous PD.docx"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville/Manager--Risk_JR-018154-1": {
      "title": "Manager, Risk",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nRole type:  Full-time; Continuing  Faculty:  Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences  Salary:  UOM 8 - $125,191 - $135,504 p.a. plus 17% super  Faculty risk expert role / integrate risk culture through stakeholder influence  Bring your enterprise risk expertise to a new team and apply now to shape MDHS’s future.   Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.     The University of Melbourne    We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research.  Discover more via our website.   Your next career opportunity    You will lead enterprise risk, compliance and business continuity across MDHS as the Faculty’s expert advisor.  You will shape practical frameworks, uplift risk capability, and support informed decision making for diverse stakeholders.  You will enjoy autonomy within a new, integrated team, influencing culture across complex clinical and academic environments.   What you will deliver:    Lead implementation and continuous improvement of MDHS organizational and enterprise risk, compliance and business continuity frameworks.  Support Schools and teams to identify, assess, treat and monitor diverse strategic, operational and partnership risks.  Develop risk registers, reporting and insights using ERMS to inform MDHS leadership and governance forums.  Build strong stakeholder relationships and networks, driving engagement, training and communication on risk and compliance.  Identify and deliver continuous improvement initiatives to simplify processes and integrate risk with planning and performance     You may be a great fit if you:    Hold a relevant tertiary qualification and substantial experience in enterprise risk within large, complex organisations.  Have demonstrated experience in strategic, operational, research, education, clinical partnership, compliance and reputational risk management.  Demonstrate deep knowledge of ISO 31000 and practical application of recognised risk management frameworks.  Translate policy and governance requirements into user-focused processes, guidance and tools that uplift risk capability.  Excel at stakeholder engagement, building influence across diverse academic, professional and clinical partner groups.  Manage competing priorities in a matrix environment, applying strong analytical, problem-solving and communication skills.  Use risk, compliance and reporting systems confidently, ideally with experience in higher education or regulated environments.  For further information please refer to the attached PD.   What we offer you!    We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:   Build future financial security with 17% superannuation  Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being   Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning  Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave  Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company   Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program   For more information check out our benefits page!    Your new team – Faculty of Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences   Your new team sits within the Faculty of Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences, Australia’s leader in clinical and health sciences. You will join a newly formed, integrated risk function that partners closely with Schools, research institutes and major clinical organisations. Together, you will strengthen governance, resilience and risk culture across a large, distributed faculty, working with passionate colleagues committed to impactful education, research and community health..   Be Yourself    The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences.  Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb.   We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities.  Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process.   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants    We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our  Indigenous staff page  to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.        Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at  korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au .   Application essentials:   Visit  \"apply with us\"  to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.  You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.  A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.   Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process.   Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria below - no more than 2 pages:  1. Demonstrated experience in enterprise risk management within a large, complex organisation, including risk identification, assessment, treatment, monitoring and reporting using recognised risk management frameworks  2. Demonstrated understanding of ISO 31000 Risk Management Standard, organisational, strategic and enterprise risk management principles, frameworks and methodologies and their practical application in operational environments.  3. Proven ability to translate policy and frameworks into practical, user-focused processes and guidance.  4. Demonstrated experience supporting organisational risk governance, risk reporting and risk assurance activities.  5. Excellent stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to build relationships and influence across a diverse organisation.  6. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively in a matrix environment and manage competing priorities.  Want to know more?   For queries related to this specific position, contact Belinda Hofmeyr (belinda.hofmeyr@unimelb.edu.au)  For questions related to our recruitment process email Vanessa Phan at  hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at  hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au  (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').   Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future.  Applications close:  16 October 2026 at 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.   Position Description:   PD_JR-018154 Manager, Risk.docx   PD_JR-018154 Manager, Risk.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville-Victoria/Research-Fellow-in-Molecular-Microbiology_JR-018543": {
      "title": "Research Fellow in Molecular Microbiology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-23\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nRole type: Full Time (1.0 FTE); Fixed-Term for 2 years  Faculty: Faculty of Science  Department/ School: School of BioSciences  Salary: Level B: $124,656 - $148,023 p.a. plus 17% super   Translational molecular microbiology focus / develop next-generation diagnostics for infectious diseases / collaborate with clinical and industry partners.   Join the Huston Lab to advance infectious disease diagnostics and accelerate your postdoctoral research career.  Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.     The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website.   Your next career opportunity   You will lead and contribute to research in molecular microbiology and infectious disease diagnostics. You will design, optimise and validate novel assays, translating microbial insights into practical clinical applications. You will collaborate across disciplines, contribute to research publications and support emerging researchers within a collaborative and supportive lab environment.  What you will deliver:    Conduct innovative molecular microbiology research on infectious diseases, particularly sexually transmitted infections, with increasing independence.  Design, develop, optimise and validate novel molecular diagnostic assays, integrating genomics and bioinformatics where appropriate.  Publish high-quality research outputs, present at conferences and contribute to competitive grant and funding applications.  Supervise and mentor undergraduate and graduate students, and support junior researchers to deliver impactful publications.  Engage with clinical, public health or industry partners to progress translational diagnostics and build collaborative networks.  You may be a great fit if you:    Hold a PhD in Microbiology, Molecular Biology, Biomedical Science or a closely related discipline.  Demonstrate strong expertise in molecular microbiology techniques including PCR, sequencing, microbial culture and molecular cloning.  Bring experience developing, optimising or validating molecular diagnostic assays for infectious diseases or related biomedical applications.  Maintain a strong publication record and communicate research findings clearly through manuscripts, reports and conference presentations.  Manage projects effectively, working both independently and within multidisciplinary teams to meet deadlines and research goals.  Apply or develop genomics, bioinformatics or advanced molecular data analysis skills relevant to pathogen detection and characterisation.  For further information please refer to the attached PD.   What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:   Build future financial security with 17% superannuation  Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being   Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning  Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave  Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company   Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program     For more information check out our benefits page!   Your new team – School of BioSciences   You will join the School of BioSciences, a vibrant hub tackling major global biological challenges. Our researchers span ecology, evolution, genetics, genomics and molecular systems biology, fostering rich cross-disciplinary collaborations. Within the Faculty of Science, you will access world-class facilities, platforms and well-supported research networks. We value curiosity, excellence, impact and integrity, and offer an inclusive environment where diverse perspectives thrive.  Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb.   We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process.   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.        Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at oied-hr@unimelb.edu.au .   Application essentials:   Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.  You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.   A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.   Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process.   Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description.  Want to know more?   For queries related to this specific position, contact Willa Huston at willa.huston@unimelb.edu.au    For questions related to our recruitment process email Oliver Bukasa at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').     Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future.  Applications close: 14 O ctober 2026 at 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.   Position Description:    JR-018543 - Research Fellow in Molecular Microbiology - PD.docx   JR-018543 - Research Fellow in Molecular Microbiology - PD.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville/Postdoctoral-Research-Fellow---Research-Fellow---Senior-Research-Fellow_JR-018549": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow / Research Fellow / Senior Research Fellow",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nRole type:  Full time, Fixed-term until November 2027 (part-time considered) Faculty: Faculty of Engineering and Information Technology Salary: Level A - $87,266 - $118,416 p.a. plus 17% super  Level B - $124,656 - $148,023 p.a. plus 17% super  Level C - $152,695 - $176,065 p.a. plus 17% super  Work on secure containment for AI agents atop seL4 / collaborate with world-leading formal methods experts / shape next-generation AI-assisted verification tools Apply now to help build safer AI systems and advanced verification methods within a dynamic international research team. Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.  The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. Your next career opportunity   You will join an international project securing AI agents using formally verified seL4-based reference monitors. You will develop AI-assisted verification techniques and contribute to large-scale Isabelle/HOL proof engineering. You will also gain experience supervising students and collaborating across academia, government and industry. What you will deliver:   Advance research on secure AI containment by designing and verifying seL4-based reference monitors and mechanisms. Develop AI-assisted verification methods and AI proof agents to support large-scale Isabelle/HOL proof maintenance and evolution. Publish high-quality research, present findings at leading conferences, and contribute to collaborative project reports and deliverables. Supervise and mentor students and junior researchers, fostering capability in formal methods and automated reasoning. Collaborate with national and international partners, and contribute to grant proposals, outreach and broader departmental activities. You may be a great fit if you:   Hold a PhD in formal methods, automated reasoning, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrate a strong publication record in leading venues, commensurate with experience and opportunity. Bring expertise in areas such as interactive theorem proving, formal verification, security foundations or AI-assisted reasoning. Exhibit excellent analytical, problem-solving and data management skills, with meticulous research record keeping. Communicate complex concepts clearly to technical and non-technical audiences, both in writing and in person. Thrive in collaborative, multi-disciplinary teams and show initiative in leading projects or supervising students. For further information please refer to the attached PD.  What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:  Build future financial security with 17% superannuation Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being  Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company  Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program  For more information check out our benefits page!  Your new team – Faculty of Engineering and Information Technology You will join the Faculty of Engineering and Information Technology’s vibrant formal methods and security community. Our researchers collaborate across computing, AI and systems to build trustworthy, high-assurance technologies with real-world impact. You will work closely with leading academics and international partners on the Agentic seL4 project. Benefit from strong mentoring, seminar programmes and access to advanced tools, infrastructure and collaborative networks. Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.    Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au . Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. Visa sponsorship is possible; however preference will be given to candidates who can start immediately. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process. Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description. Want to know more? For queries related to this specific position, contact Toby Murray at toby.murray@unimelb.edu.au For questions related to our recruitment process email Nick Petersen at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments'). Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future. Applications close: Saturday October 24 at 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.  Position Descriptions Word: Postdoctoral Research Fellow (Toby Murray) PD.docx PDF: Postdoctoral Research Fellow (Toby Murray) PD.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville/Research-Fellow---Clinical-Diagnostic-Translation-Research_JR-018362": {
      "title": "Research Fellow – Clinical Diagnostic Translation Research",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nRole type:  Full Time, Fixed Term for 12 months Faculty: Medicine, Dentistry & Health Sciences Department/ School:  Department of Infectious Diseases Salary: Level A - $87,266 - $118,416 or Level B $124,656 - $148,023 p.a. plus 17% super  Multidisciplinary infectious diseases diagnostics research / real-world clinical and self-collection implementation / national and international field study leadership Join our team to shape future STI diagnostics through impactful translational research and strong clinical partnerships. Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.  The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. Your next career opportunity   You will lead clinical diagnostic implementation studies that improve STI detection and care in real-world settings. You will design and deliver multi-site trials, engaging clinicians, laboratories and health services across Australia and internationally. You will gain mentoring within a collaborative team, building a strong track record in translational infectious diseases research. What you will deliver:   Lead design and delivery of diagnostic implementation studies, including multi-site STI point-of-care trial expansion and monitoring. Develop study protocols, ethics submissions and regulatory documentation, ensuring compliance and robust governance across all projects. Coordinate participant recruitment, data collection and qualitative and quantitative analysis with clinical and laboratory collaborators. Train and support site staff in research procedures and diagnostic testing, providing remote oversight of study conduct. Mentor students and junior researchers, contribute to manuscripts and presentations, and participate actively in laboratory meetings.   You may be a great fit if:   Hold a PhD in a relevant discipline or equivalent experience in implementation or infectious diseases research. Bring experience co-designing and delivering research with health services, diagnostic laboratories, clinicians and consumers. Demonstrate expertise implementing medical technologies, ideally diagnostics, within complex multi-stakeholder clinical and laboratory environments. Possess a strong track record in clinical research, including ethics applications, data management and mixed-methods analysis. Excel at managing competing priorities while mentoring junior colleagues and maintaining meticulous project documentation and records. Commit to high scientific and ethical standards and to building effective collaborations with diverse external partners. For further information please refer to the attached PD.  What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:  Build future financial security with 17% superannuation Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being  Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company  Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program  For more information check out our benefits page!  Your new team – You will join the Pasricha Laboratory within the Department of Infectious Diseases at the Doherty Institute. Our team brings together clinician-scientists, basic scientists, epidemiologists, and public health professionals. We focus on antimicrobial resistance, sexually transmissible infections, HIV, and emerging infections. You will benefit from a collaborative, mentoring-oriented culture that supports impactful translational diagnostics research and career development. Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.    Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au   Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process. Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description. Want to know more? For queries related to this specific position, contact Shivani Pasricha by emailing Shivani.pasricha@unimelb.edu.au For questions related to our recruitment process email Walid at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments'). Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future. Applications close: 8 October. 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.  Position Description:   JR-018362 Research Fellow – Clinical Diagnostic Translation Research PD.pdf JR-018362 Research Fellow – Clinical Diagnostic Translation Research PD.docx"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Werribee/Clinical-Skills-Support-Nurse_JR-018146": {
      "title": "Clinical Skills Support Nurse",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-24\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nRole type: Full-time; Fixed Term until 31/12/2027 Faculty: Science School: Melbourne Veterinary School Salary: UoM 4: $80,400 – $85,328 p.a. plus 17% super Pivotal role shaping DVM clinical skills / varied multi-species work across leading veterinary sites / supportive expert team Bring your veterinary nursing expertise to empower DVM students and strengthen clinical teaching across Melbourne Veterinary School. Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.  The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. Your next career opportunity   You will support DVM students to build essential clinical skills through supervised rotations and practical teaching activities. You will work across leading clinical sites, guiding safe animal handling and nursing practices in multi-species settings. You will join an experienced, collaborative team that values innovation in veterinary education and continuous professional growth. What you will deliver:   Provide practical support to DVM students during clinical rotations at Greencross Veterinary Hospital and The Lost Dogs’ Home. Assemble and support clinical skills training, assessments and simulation-based teaching across key veterinary species and procedures. Prepare and maintain anaesthesia, surgical teaching and animal handling resources, ensuring equipment, models and stock meet best-practice standards. Uphold animal care ethics, patient safety and infection-control requirements, supporting veterinarians and students before and after surgery. Build strong relationships with clinical partners, contribute to service improvements, and participate in governance, meetings and training. You may be a great fit if you:   Hold a Certificate IV in Veterinary Nursing or equivalent, with proven experience in clinical veterinary practice. Demonstrate confidence in handling cats, dogs and horses, and assisting safely with a range of clinical procedures. Support training and supervision of students or staff, preferably within veterinary clinical skills or teaching environments. Manage clinical spaces, equipment, medicines and consumables, maintaining accurate patient records and documentation to high standards. Apply Occupational Health and Safety practices in clinical settings, prioritising animal welfare, student safety and regulatory compliance. Embrace working across multiple sites and rotations, adapting to changing demands and collaborating within an experienced multidisciplinary team. For further information please refer to the attached PD.  What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:  Build future financial security with 17% superannuation Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being  Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company  Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program  For more information check out our benefits page!  Your new team – Melbourne Veterinary School The Melbourne Veterinary School, part of the Faculty of Science, is Australia’s number one ranked veterinary school. We deliver Victoria’s only professional entry veterinary medicine program, grounded in strong industry partnerships and impactful clinical education. Within the School, the clinical teaching support team offers over 160 years of combined, multi-species experience. You will join a collaborative, versatile group that values curiosity, sharing ideas and continually improving veterinary teaching and patient care.  Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.    Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au . Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process. Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description. Learn more about responding to Selection Criteria Want to know more? For queries related to this specific position, contact Maddi Taper (details in PD) For questions related to our recruitment process email Lachlan Bryce at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments'). Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future. Applications close: 18 October 2026 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.  Position Description:   JR-018146 Clinical Skills Support Nurse_PD.pdf JR-018146 Clinical Skills Support Nurse_PD.docx"
