    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville-Victoria/Data-Engineer_JR-018268": {
      "title": "Data Engineer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRole type: Full-time; Fixed term to 30 June 2028, externally funded Faculty: Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences Department: Australian BioCommons Salary: UOM 8 - $125,191 - $135,504 p.a. plus 17% superannuation Shape national human genomics data infrastructure / develop broad data engineering expertise / join a supportive, close-knit team Apply now to help researchers securely unlock complex human genomics data for real-world health impact. Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities. The University of Melbourne We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. Your next career opportunity In this role, you will engineer secure, well-governed data commons for sensitive human genomics research. You will work end-to-end across data operations, whether your background is academic, industry or government. You will develop versatile technical skills while contributing to nationally significant research infrastructure and health-focused projects. What you will deliver: Design and maintain high-quality data dictionaries, submission templates and harmonisation approaches for human genomics and multi-omics datasets. Collaborate with researchers and data managers to understand incoming data, clarify requirements and improve data quality and consistency. Develop, run and refine data transformation, validation, quality-control and migration workflows for sensitive research data holdings. Configure and operate Gen3 data commons platforms, including dictionary deployment, data ingestion, indexing and user exploration interfaces. Build tools, scripts, documentation and standard procedures that support reproducible data operations and reduce manual effort.   You may be a great fit if you: Hold a bachelor’s degree in data science, computer science, bioinformatics or a closely related discipline. Bring experience in data management, data analysis, data engineering or software development within technical environments. Demonstrate capability working carefully with structured data, including modelling, transformation, validation, harmonisation or quality assurance. Use shell, Python, R, SQL or similar tools in cloud or server environments to manage datasets. Understand data security and privacy considerations when retaining, accessing and using potentially sensitive human research data. Thrive in collaborative projects, communicating clearly with technical and non-technical stakeholders and taking ownership of tasks.   For further information please refer to the attached PD. What we offer you! We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including: Build future financial security with 17% superannuation Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave, cultural leave, and menstruation and menopause leave. Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program For more information check out our benefits page! Your new team – Australian BioCommons You will join Australian BioCommons, a national NCRIS-funded research infrastructure program hosted by the University. Working in a close-knit team of around ten specialists, you will collaborate across institutions and disciplines. The Human Genome Informatics division builds secure, scalable data platforms that underpin cutting-edge human genomics and multi-omics research. You will be part of a collaborative, learning-focused environment committed to practical impact and responsible data stewardship. Be Yourself The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.    Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au . Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process. You are not required to address the Selection Criteria for this application. Want to know more? For questions related to our recruitment process email Alex Spezza at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments'). Apply today and join a community that’s shaping the future. Applications close: Wednesday 14th of October 2026 at 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone. Position Description: JR-018268 - Data Engineer - PD.pdf JR-018268 - Data Engineer - PD.docx"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville-Victoria/Research-Security-Leader_JR-018634-1": {
      "title": "Research Security Leader",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRole type: Full-time; Continuing  Department: MRE – Office of Research Ethics and Integrity  Salary: UOM 9 - $146,049 - $151,951 p.a. plus 17% super  Strategic research security leadership role / shape compliant global collaborations and protect University reputation / partner with senior academics, regulators and government  Apply now to lead a high-performing research security team and influence secure, responsible research across the University.  Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.      The University of Melbourne    We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website.   Your next career opportunity:   You will lead a specialist research security team supporting secure, compliant and impactful research collaborations.  You will advise on complex national security, export controls and foreign interference risks across a leading research-intensive university.  You will shape education, guidance and policy that strengthen research integrity and protect the University’s global reputation.  What you will deliver:   Lead and mentor Research Security Advisors to deliver high-quality, timely advice and support to researchers.  Oversee allocation, workflow and prioritisation across the team, balancing reactive requests and proactive compliance initiatives.  Provide expert guidance on complex research security matters, including export controls, sanctions and foreign interference obligations.  Monitor emerging geopolitical, research security and cybersecurity risks, and translate insights into strengthened protections and practices.  Develop and deliver training, briefings and communications, and represent the University in engagements with regulators and sector forums.    You may be a great fit if you:   Hold postgraduate qualifications in a relevant discipline, or equivalent experience in research, security or compliance.  Demonstrate deep knowledge of research security, foreign interference guidance and related legislation affecting the university sector.  Apply advanced analytical thinking and sound judgement to complex, sensitive and ethical research risk scenarios.  Communicate complex regulatory and security concepts clearly through training, briefings, outreach and written guidance.  Lead and develop staff, drive efficient team operations and build strong relationships across diverse stakeholder groups.  Draft regulatory submissions, engage confidently with government and regulators, and remain curious about emerging research security issues.    What we offer you!    We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:   Build future financial security with 17% superannuation  Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being   Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning  Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave  Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company   Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program   For more information check out our benefits page!      Your new team:   Melbourne Research & Enterprise supports researchers to secure funding, translate discoveries and deliver real-world impact. Within this division, the Office of Research Ethics and Integrity leads governance, ethics, integrity and research security frameworks. You will join a collaborative, service-oriented team that partners with academics, professional staff, institutes and government. The team values integrity, responsiveness and continuous improvement, offering rich exposure to complex national security issues and sector-leading practice.   Be Yourself    The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb.   We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process.   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants    We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.        Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au .   Application essentials:   Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.  You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.   A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.   Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process.     Want to know more?   For queries related to this specific position, contact Mel Green  at mel.green@unimelb.edu.au    For questions related to our recruitment process email Alessandro Storani at Alessandro.storani@unimelb.edu.au    For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').     Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future.  Applications close: ​ Wednesday 21 October 2026 -11:55 PM ; Melbourne time zone.   Position Description:    PD_JR-018634 Research Security Leader .pdf PD_JR-018634 Research Security Leader .docx"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville-Victoria/Facilities-Specialist-Lead--Peter-Doherty-Institute_JR-017797-1": {
      "title": "Facilities Specialist Lead, Peter Doherty Institute",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRole type: Full-time; Continuing  Department: Campus Operations & Delivery, Enterprise Services Group  Salary: UOM 8 - AUD $125,191 - $135,504 p.a. plus 17% super  Influential facilities management leadership in world-class infectious disease institute / safeguard complex containment facilities / expanding remit including AIID  Apply now to lead critical facilities that enable cutting-edge infectious disease research and care.  Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.   The University of Melbourne    We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website.   Your next career opportunity:   In this role, you will lead the Doherty Engineering Group supporting a world-class infectious diseases institute.  You will oversee complex building services, safeguard high-containment laboratories and shape systems for the future AIID facility.  What you will deliver:   Lead and develop the Doherty Engineering Group, fostering collaboration and high-quality support for diverse bio-research professionals.  Coordinate facilities management, maintenance and engineering activities to support Joint Venture objectives and Institute teaching and research.  Identify and mitigate infrastructure risks, ensuring safety, compliance, business continuity and accurate engineering documentation.  Manage asset monitoring systems, long-term replacement planning and annual operational budgets for building services and equipment.  Oversee consultants, contractors and lease obligations, representing COD in key committees and driving continuous operational improvement.  You may be a great fit if you:   Hold a degree in engineering or equivalent experience and technical aptitude in facilities management within in a complex building environment.  Lead and contribute to an operationally focussed facilities teams within large, technically complex buildings, ideally health, hospital or laboratory settings.  Apply strong project and contractor management skills, including risk assessment and root cause analysis.  Demonstrate broad technical aptitude across mechanical, electrical, hydraulic and laboratory engineering services and control systems.  Use digital control systems and information management tools confidently to monitor, document and improve building performance.  Have excellent interpersonal and communication skills with a demonstrated ability to engage with a range of building stakeholders.  Manage operational budgets and financial reporting, including building outgoings and cost-saving opportunities.  What we offer you!    We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:   Build future financial security with 17% superannuation  Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being   Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning  Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave  Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company   Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program   For more information check out our benefits page!    Your new team:   Campus Operations & Delivery sits within the Enterprise Services Group, supporting over 600 buildings across the University.  At the Peter Doherty Institute, you will join a specialised facilities team enabling infectious disease research and care.  You will collaborate with University and health partners, shaping high-containment infrastructure and future operations for the AIID facility.  Be Yourself    The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb.   We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process.   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants    We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.        Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au   Application essentials:   Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.  You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.   A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.   Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process.   Want to know more?   For queries related to this specific position, contact Brian Cullen at cullen.b@unimelb.edu.au    For questions related to our recruitment process email Alessandro Storani at alessandro.storani@unimelb.edu.au    For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').   Apply today and join a community that’s shaping the future.  Applications close: ​Wednesday 21 October 2026 - 11:55 PM ; Melbourne time zone.   Position Description:   PD_JR-017797 Facilities Specialist Lead – Peter Doherty Institute.docx  PD_JR-017797 Facilities Specialist Lead – Peter Doherty Institute.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville-Victoria/Operations-Manager--Melbourne-National-Security-and-Defence_JR-019056": {
      "title": "Operations Manager, Melbourne National Security and Defence",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRole type: Full-time; Fixed-term (2 years)  Department: Chancellery – Melbourne Research and Enterprise  Salary: UOM 10 - $156,480 p.a. plus 17% super  Institution-wide leadership on national security and defence / shape new governance and operating frameworks / high-visibility senior role  Join us to build a resilient, secure University and lead operational excellence across national security initiatives.  Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.   The University of Melbourne    We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website.   Your next career opportunity:   In this senior role, you will establish and lead the operating framework for Melbourne National Security and Defence (MNSD). Reporting to the Associate Director, Research Collaboration, you will work closely with the MNSD Executive Director and specialist University teams, to support effective governance, risk management and compliance for complex, sensitive activities. You will assist coordinated engagement with government, industry and research partners to strengthen the University's defence capabilities.   What you will deliver:   Provide strategic operational leadership for MNSD, developing and implementing its architecture, operating framework and core activities.  Oversee day-to-day operations, workflows and resourcing across national security and defence initiatives, aligning activity with University priorities.  Lead governance, risk and compliance processes, ensuring robust controls and adherence to DISP and institutional frameworks.  Build strong relationships with senior leaders, academic staff and partners, acting as a trusted operational point of contact.  Drive continuous improvement in service models, reporting, performance measures and ways of working across MNSD and partner teams.  You may be a great fit if you:   Hold a postgraduate qualification and extensive experience in large-scale project or operations management at corporate level.  Operate effectively at senior management level, cultivating relationships and engaging diverse stakeholders in complex environments.  Demonstrate strong expertise in governance, risk and compliance within large, complex or highly regulated organisations.  Coordinate activity across multiple portfolios or functions, managing interdependencies to achieve whole-of-organisation outcomes.  Produce clear, persuasive operational reports, briefings and advice for governance committees and executive audiences.  Bring understanding of the defence and national security research environment, including associated risks, opportunities and compliance expectations.  What we offer you!    We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:   Build future financial security with 17% superannuation  Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being   Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning  Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave  Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company   Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program   For more information check out our benefits page!    Your new team: You will join Melbourne Research and Enterprise within Chancellery, supporting the University’s ambition to translate research excellence into societal benefit.  Melbourne National Security and Defence brings together strategic governance, institutional coordination and partner engagement to strengthen the University’s contribution to national security and defence. It connects expertise across the University, supports priority research capabilities and helps coordinate engagement with government, industry and higher education partners. Working closely with the MNSD Executive Director and reporting to the Associate Director, Research Collaboration, you will help build the operational foundations of this initiative.    Be Yourself    The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb.   We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process.   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants    We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.   Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au .   Application essentials:   Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.  You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.   You will need to be eligible to hold an appropriate Australian Government security clearance.   A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.   Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process.   You are not required to address the Selection Criteria for this application. Want to know more?   For queries related to this specific position, contact Michael Webb at m.webb@unimelb.edu.au    For questions related to our recruitment process email Alessandro Storani at Alessandro.storani@unimelb.edu.au    For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').   Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future.  Applications close: ​ Sunday 18 October 2026 - 11:55 PM ; Melbourne time zone.   Position Description:    PD_JR-019056 Operations Manager, Melbourne National Security and Defence.docx PD_JR-019056 Operations Manager, Melbourne National Security and Defence.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville-Victoria/Senior-Advisor--Gender-Based-Violence_JR-017963-1": {
      "title": "Senior Advisor: Gender-Based Violence",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-06\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Number: JR-017963   Role type: Full-time; Continuing  Department/School: Student and Scholarly Services  Salary: UOM 8 - AUD $125,191 - $135,504 p.a. plus 17% super  Specialist trauma-informed role supporting victim survivors / shape University-wide gender-based violence responses / influence safer campus culture  Apply to use your gender-based violence expertise to support our community and strengthen institutional responses.  Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.   The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website.   Your next career opportunity   You will provide specialist, trauma-informed support to students and staff impacted by gender-based violence. You will guide colleagues and influence safer practices across the University’s Safer Community Program. You will deepen your expertise applying national codes and risk frameworks in a complex, values-driven setting.   What you will deliver:    Provide trauma-informed responses to disclosures and reports of gender-based violence from students and staff.  Connect impacted community members with specialist services and complaint processes within and external to the University.  Assess risk, escalate urgent or complex matters, and contribute to coordinated safety planning across the University.  Deliver capacity-building workshops and secondary consultations to strengthen colleagues’ confidence responding to gender-based violence.  Maintain high-quality, confidential case records and support continuous improvement of Safer Community Program practices.  You may be a great fit if you:    Hold a tertiary qualification in Social Work or an equivalent combination of education and experience.  Demonstrate advanced, trauma-informed practice with victim survivors and understanding of support models for perpetrators.  Bring strong knowledge of gender-based violence risk assessment, safety planning and relevant police and court processes.  Understand the National Higher Education Code and university reporting and complaint processes, or quickly learn this context.  Excel at building constructive relationships with diverse stakeholders in large, complex organisations.  Produce clear, sensitive written documentation, including detailed case notes and accurate information management records.  For further information please refer to the attached PD.   What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:   Build future financial security with 17% superannuation  Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being   Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning  Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave  Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company   Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program   For more information check out our benefits page!   Your new team – Student and Scholarly Services   You will join Student and Scholarly Services within the Chief Operating Officer Portfolio, a collaborative team that supports students from first enquiry to graduation. The Safer Community Program leads University-wide responses to concerning, threatening and harmful behaviours, partnering closely with faculties and central divisions. You will work with committed professionals who value evidence-informed practice, prevention and early intervention, and who are focused on building a safer, more respectful environment for every member of the University community.   Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb.   We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process.   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.        Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au .   Application essentials:   Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.  You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.  A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.   Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process.   Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria , found in the Position Description below  Want to know more?   For questions related to our recruitment process email Tien Nguyen at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').   Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future.  Applications close: Tuesday, 20th October 2026, at 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.   Position Description:    PD_JR-017963 Senior Advisor Gender-Based Violence.docx   PD_JR-017963 Senior Advisor Gender-Based Violence.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville/Research-Fellow-in-Microbial-Fluid-Dynamics_JR-018985": {
      "title": "Research Fellow in Microbial Fluid Dynamics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-06\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRole type: Full-time; Fixed term (2 years) Faculty: Science Department/School: School of Mathematics and Statistics Salary: Level A: $87,266 - $118,416 p.a. plus 17% super ARC-funded microbial fluid dynamics role / explore how flows shape microbial behaviour and signalling / join a top applied mathematics group. Apply now to drive pioneering microbial fluid dynamics research and contribute to world-class applied mathematics teaching. Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.  The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. Your next career opportunity   You will lead innovative research on microscale fluid dynamics that explains how flows shape microbial movement and communication. You will combine mathematical modelling, computation and collaboration to produce high-impact publications and support student learning. What you will deliver:   Lead research on microbial fluid dynamics in unconfined and confined flows aligned with the ARC Future Fellowship. Develop and analyse mathematical and computational models of cell motility, navigation and micro-scale chemical interactions. Publish high-quality papers, present at conferences, and contribute to competitive research funding proposals. Teach one Applied Mathematics subject per year or equivalent, and support student supervision and mentoring. Engage with collaborators, participate in School activities, and promote the University’s research profile and values. You may be a great fit if you:   Hold a completed or near-completed PhD in Applied Mathematics or a closely related discipline. Demonstrate a strong research track record in areas aligned with fluid dynamics or cell motility. Bring experience in continuum or agent-based modelling and in developing computational simulations. Collaborate effectively within multidisciplinary teams and contribute positively to a collegial research culture. Communicate research clearly through publications, presentations, and engagement with diverse internal and external audiences. Offer desirable strengths such as high-performance computing, teaching experience or familiarity with experimental biophysics. For further information please refer to the attached PD.  What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:  Build future financial security with 17% superannuation Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being  Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave, cultural leave, and menstruation and menopause leave. Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company  Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program  For more information check out our benefits page!  Your new team – School of Mathematics and Statistics The School of Mathematics and Statistics is one of Australia’s premier mathematics communities, renowned for excellence in research, teaching and engagement. Home to a large, diverse cohort of academics, researchers and students, the School sustains a vibrant culture of seminars, collaborations and international partnerships. Within this, the Melbourne Applied Mathematics and Mathematical Biology Group brings together experts in fluid dynamics, mathematical biology and computation to tackle complex biological and physical systems. Supported by strong ARC funding and research infrastructure, the group offers an intellectually rich, collegial environment with deep connections across science and industry.  Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.    Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au . Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process. Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description. Learn more about responding to Selection Criteria Want to know more? For queries related to this specific position, contact Douglas Brumley (details in PD) For questions related to our recruitment process email Lachlan Bryce at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments'). Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future. Applications close: 20 October 2026 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.  Position Description:     JR-018985 Research Fellow in Microbial Fluid Dynamics_PD.pdf JR-018985 Research Fellow in Microbial Fluid Dynamics_PD.docx"
    }
  },
